## Read before your first edit

1. `docs/README.md` — the standards hierarchy and what each `status` means.
2. The documents for the layers your change touches. Only `ratified` documents are binding.
   A `proposed` document is a default not yet adopted; a `not-started` one has no rules —
   **never infer a rule from it, ask.**
3. For implementation work: the story spec and its parent feature spec
   (`docs/17-specs/spec-lifecycle.md`).
4. `docs/16-ai/` — what you may do on your own, what needs approval, and what is prohibited.

## Bootstrap state

If `docs/01-business/principles.md` is not `ratified`, this project has not been bootstrapped.
Before anything else, run the **bootstrap-project** skill
(`.agents/skills/bootstrap-project/SKILL.md`) or ask the user to.

## Skills

Skills are procedures in `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. When a task matches one, read that
file and follow it. Reference other skills by path, never by a tool's command syntax.

